[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   Step 112 -- OSSOS characterized-ensemble audit.
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   Every resident-signature test so far runs on survey samples whose
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   selection functions must be modelled from proxy data (designation
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   half-months, calibrated smearing widths).  The Outer Solar System
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   Origins Survey ensemble (Bannister et al. 2018, ApJS 236, 18; VizieR
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   J/ApJS/236/18/t3char) is the only large TNO sample that is fully
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   characterized by construction: 840 objects with secure multi-opposition
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   orbits, the survey's own dynamical classification, and -- decisive for
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   this audit -- the exact discovery astrometry (RA, Dec, JD) of every
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   object in the same table.  The discovery geometry here is measured,
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   not proxied.
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   This step scores the ensemble against the pre-declared axis
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   (lam, beta) = (49 deg, -17 deg), cap 60 deg:
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   1.  Per-class selectivity profile.  OSSOS labels each object cen /
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   sca / det / res / cla / jco.  The TEP resident signature is claimed
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   to live on boundary-crossing detached orbits; the characterized
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   ensemble tests that claim class-by-class under one selection
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   function.
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   2.  Class-aware footprint baselines.  The discovery-longitude --
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   longitude-of-perihelion coupling is not universal: eccentric
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   populations (det, sca, cen) are discovered preferentially near
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   perihelion, so varpi tracks the discovery longitude lam_disc with
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   the measured ~50 deg smear; low-eccentricity and resonant
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   populations (cla, res, jco) are discovered at any orbital phase,
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   so varpi is decoupled from lam_disc and the correct baseline is
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   uniform (cap fraction 1/3).  The coupling is measured directly
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   here -- the resultant of varpi - lam_disc per class -- rather than
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   assumed, which also cross-validates the pipeline's footprint model
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   on independent data.
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   3.  Detached-cohort audit.  The 31 'det' objects: in-cap fraction
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   versus uniform (1/3), versus the coupled-footprint baseline
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   (smeared-cap model with the SBDB-measured 50 deg width), and
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   versus the registered P1 prediction (0.59); secure-flagged subset;
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   discovery-sector split; strict a>150, q>30 subset; a-stratified
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   trend; element-uncertainty propagation (published sigma_Omega,
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   sigma_omega jittered into cap membership); and the inter-fitter
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   floor against the SBDB orbit record.
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   4.  Resonant positive control.  The 132 plutinos carry a known
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   Neptune-organized varpi structure (apsidal libration avoids the
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   conjunction geometry).  Neptune's osculating longitude of
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   perihelion is computed from DE440s on the same machinery the
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   N-body steps use; the plutino separation distribution is compared
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   against it -- the machinery must recover known solar-system
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   structure before an anomalous structure can be credited.
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   Honest reading: the OSSOS 'det' class is dominated by semimajor axes
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   of ~50-90 AU -- inside the ~150 AU boundary the resident signature
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   occupies -- so the cohort is primarily a selectivity and
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   selection-function control, not a high-leverage replication; the
[2026-09-21 15:12:44 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 112]   strict a>150 members are reported for the record.
